<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="correction"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Arthritis Res Ther</journal-id><journal-title>Arthritis Research &#x00026; Therapy</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">1478-6354</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1478-6362</issn><publisher><publisher-name>BioMed Central</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2688238</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="publisher-id">ar2593</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/ar2593</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Correction</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Correction: What magnetic resonance imaging has told us about the pathogenesis of rheumatoid arthritis &#x02013; the first 50 years</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib id="A1" corresp="yes" contrib-type="author"><name><surname>McGonagle</surname><given-names>Dennis</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1">1</xref><email>d.g.mcgonagle@leeds.ac.uk</email></contrib><contrib id="A2" contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>Ai Lyn</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="I1">1</xref></contrib></contrib-group><aff id="I1"><label>1</label>Academic Unit of Musculoskeletal Disease, University of Leeds and Chapel Allerton Hospital, Chapeltown Road, Leeds, LS7 4SA, UK</aff><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><year>2009</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="epub"><day>22</day><month>1</month><year>2009</year></pub-date><volume>11</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>401</fpage><lpage>401</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://arthritis-research.com/content/11/1/401"/><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright &#x000a9; 2009 BioMed Central Ltd</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2009</copyright-year><copyright-holder>BioMed Central Ltd</copyright-holder></permissions><related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="10" page="222" id="N0x3219e40N0x4068980" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="18947372" ext-link-type="pubmed"/></article-meta><notes><p>See related review by McGonagle and Tan, <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://arthritis-research.com/content/10/5/222"/></p></notes></front><body><p>After publication of our recent article [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B1">1</xref>], we noticed an error in the legend of figure 2:</p><p>"The marrow soft tissues have an increased water content due to the osteitis that is seen as a high signal on fat suppression MRI (grey squares), as shown in (b)."</p><p>This sentence should refer to panel (b) in figure 1. The correct sentence is:</p><p>The marrow soft tissues have an increased water content due to the osteitis that is seen as a high signal on fat suppression MRI (grey squares), as shown in figure 1(b).</p></body><back><ref-list><ref id="B1"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McGonagle</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Tan</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>What magnetic resonance imaging has told us about the pathogenesis of rheumatoid arthritis &#x02013; the first 50 years</article-title><source>Arthritis Res Ther</source><year>2008</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>222</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18947372</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/ar2512</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>